@* A render island for markup that changes several times a second (a game HUD strip, a
   status chip). The page writes the markup as ChildContent, so it keeps reading the page's
   own fields and keeps the page's scoped CSS, but a per-tick update calls Refresh() on this
   region instead of StateHasChanged() on the page: only the region's subtree is diffed, not
   the page, its GameShell and every panel around them. A normal page render still flows
   through (ChildContent is a new fragment each time), so nothing goes stale.

   Adds no DOM of its own. *@
@ChildContent

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public RenderFragment ChildContent { get; set; } = default!;

    /// <summary>Re-render just this region (safe to call from any interop callback).</summary>
    public void Refresh() => _ = InvokeAsync(StateHasChanged);
}
